<% content_for :title, "Analyze a video of #{@carousel.name}" %>
<p class="muted"><%= link_to @carousel.name, @carousel %></p>
<h1>Analyze a video</h1>
<p>Upload clips of the carousel turning and the tool will draft its layout: how many sections and rows,
  what each figure is, whether it's a stander or a jumper, and a short description.
  Nothing changes on the carousel until you review the draft and apply it.</p>

<section class="card prose video-recipe">
  <h2>How to film it</h2>
  <p>Film up to three clips, each a little over one full revolution. Start and end on the lead figure so the tool can tell where the loop closes.</p>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Side pass.</strong> Stand at the rail with the camera at figure height, pointed straight in at the center pole, and hold still. This shows the carved outer side of row A.</li>
    <li><strong>Oncoming pass.</strong> Stand at the rail angled about 45° toward the figures coming at you. The rows show side by side as each section approaches, which is the best view for counting rows and seeing faces.</li>
    <li><strong>Inner pass.</strong> Ride the platform, or walk it while the ride is stopped, pointing outward from the inner row so the middle and inner figures aren't hidden behind the outer ones.</li>
  </ol>
  <p><strong>Only have one video?</strong> That's fine. Take steady footage from the side, at the rail, for one or more times around, and upload it as the side pass.</p>
  <p>Film at least one clip while the ride is running, with the tops of the poles and the overhead cranks in the frame: jumper poles ride up and down on turning cranks, while stander poles stay fixed, which is how the tool tells them apart.
    Use landscape, the 1x lens (no ultrawide or zoom), 1080p at 30 fps, and keep the camera steady instead of following figures.</p>
</section>

<%= form_with model: [ @carousel, @analysis ], url: carousel_video_analyses_path(@carousel), class: "form" do |form| %>
  <%= render "shared/errors", record: @analysis %>
  <% VideoAnalysis::PASSES.each do |pass, label| %>
    <div class="field">
      <%= form.label pass, label %>
      <%= form.file_field pass, accept: VideoAnalysis::VIDEO_TYPES.join(",") %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
  <p class="hint">MP4, MOV, or WebM, up to <%= number_to_human_size(VideoAnalysis::MAX_VIDEO_SIZE) %> each. One clip works; more clips give a better reading. Clips are deleted once the analysis succeeds.</p>
  <div class="actions"><%= form.submit "Upload and analyze" %> <%= link_to "Cancel", @carousel %></div>
<% end %>
